    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can create personalized math practice with instant feedback, like adaptive quizzes that adjust to a student’s level. They can also explain concepts in simple terms, breaking down complex topics into relatable examples—like comparing calculus to baking or gardening. This makes learning less intimidating and more engaging."
